{
  "meta": {
    "schema_version": "1.1",
    "study_id": "wct_glp1",
    "description": "Categorized keyword lexicon for the WCT GLP-1 study. Each category groups domain terms participants used; each keyword carries the surface variants (spellings, brand/generic pairs, plurals, phrasings) that should count toward it. build-keyword-usage.mjs matches this lexicon against segments.json and writes deterministic, reproducible counts to keyword_usage.json. Editable and versioned; bump schema_version when categories or keywords change.",
    "changelog": [
      "1.0 — initial lexicon: 7 categories, derived from participant_06, participant_09, participant_10 transcripts.",
      "1.1 — keywords and variants can be added interactively from the segment tag drawer."
    ],
    "matching_notes": [
      "Matching is case-insensitive. Within a variant, runs of spaces/hyphens match any run of whitespace or hyphens (so 'out of pocket' also matches 'out-of-pocket').",
      "Variants with no separator (e.g. 'glp1') are listed explicitly because the separator in multi-word variants is required, not optional.",
      "Brand and generic names for the same molecule are grouped under one keyword (semaglutide groups Wegovy/Ozempic; tirzepatide groups Mounjaro/Zepbound).",
      "Keywords are matched independently, so a span like 'oral GLP-1' counts toward both the 'oral_medication' and 'glp_1' keywords. Categories and keywords may therefore overlap textually; counts are not de-duplicated across keywords.",
      "Single-word terms (e.g. 'support', 'site', 'blood pressure') are precise enough for this corpus but can capture incidental uses; multi-word phrases are the most precise entries."
    ]
  },
